# __name__ configuration example.
#
# config.yml is generated locally and ignored by git; this committed example
# documents its shape. Copy it to config.yml, or let weld generate config.yml.
# The loader reads config.yml from the working directory by default; pass
# --config to point elsewhere.
#
# Precedence, highest first: command-line flag, environment variable, this file,
# built-in defaults. The database password may live in config.yml for local
# development; a production environment should override DB_PASSWORD or
# DATABASE_URL instead of committing a credential.
#
# Each capability appends only the section it needs inside the marked region.
# weld:config:begin
# weld:config:end
